<title>UK: Caledonia profits and NAV rise in H1.</title>
<headline>Caledonia profits and NAV rise in H1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		17.7		   vs 17.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 6.2		    vs 5.9</p>
<p> Pretax		     23.6		   vs 22.8</p>
<p> Net asset value(pence) 831		    vs 724</p>
<p> Turnover		   28.1		   vs 28.7</p>
<p> Tax			  8.5		    vs 7.8</p>
<p> Profit retained	  9.6		    vs 9.6</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 16, 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Dec 17</p>
<p>NOTE - Caledonia Investments Plc, a diversified trading and investment company, said the recent strength of sterling had been a welcome surprise even though the value of its overseas assets had diminished in sterling terms as a consequence.</p>
</text>
